  "method": "Calibration: x from the measured left and right body edges (columns 63 and 1698, intensity profile); y uses the same scale, because square pads (56 x 58 px) and round buttons measure within 3.5 % of square, anchored on the measured front edge (row 1127); y0 = 72 is the rear edge of the published 469.5 mm depth, derived, since the plate's visible rear edge (row 253) is 389 mm from the front and the remaining depth is the display housing. Boxes: round button = bezel outer edge; rectangular button = face outline; knob and rotary switch = cap; pad = rim outer edge; jog = outer edge of the platter ring; vertical fader = travel slot with cap width; crossfader = travel slot with cap height; slide switch = body; LOAD, BACK, TAG TRACK, TRACK FILTER and the rotary selector sit on the display assembly and are placed where the photo shows them. Deck 2 traced as deck 1 + 1053 px, checked on 12 deck-2 controls (within 1 px). Read off 2x crops with a 10 px grid; second pass on 10 controls at 4x with a 5 px grid. Independent repeat by a second reader (Sun 8 Nov 2026): d1-cue, d1-pad-1, d1-loop-in, d1-sync, ch1-eq-high, master-level, crossfader, fx-on-off, d2-tempo and browse re-read on 4x crops with a 10 px grid; centre spread at most 1.5 px (0.7 mm, crossfader), edges within 3 px.",
